WEBVTT

00:20.990 --> 00:22.370
We've cornered it.

00:22.800 --> 00:23.710
Let's begin the capture.

00:24.490 --> 00:24.860
Go!

00:38.600 --> 00:39.020
What?!

01:02.590 --> 01:04.620
I-I'm terribly sorry.

01:05.440 --> 01:06.400
We lost it.

01:07.640 --> 01:10.670
Truly, Z's power is astonishing.

01:11.610 --> 01:12.330
Search for it.

01:13.180 --> 01:16.140
For the sake of the world that we, the Flare Gang, are aiming for.

01:20.200 --> 01:25.950
The Explosive Birth of Z!
That Which Lies Hidden in Kalos!!

01:29.410 --> 01:30.640
Here goes!

01:32.800 --> 01:40.770
With the one Gym badge still needed to participate in the Kalos League in sight, Satoshi was continuing his journey to Eisetsu City with his friends.

01:48.320 --> 01:49.600
We are leaving, Eureka.

01:50.880 --> 01:52.570
It won't be long until we reach the Pokémon Center.

01:52.910 --> 01:53.310
Yeah!

02:00.700 --> 02:02.030
Eureka, what's the matter?

02:02.400 --> 02:03.740
Something's in here!

02:04.080 --> 02:04.450
What?

02:13.340 --> 02:14.330
Whoa!

02:15.760 --> 02:16.690
It moved!

02:19.170 --> 02:20.220
Wait!

02:20.910 --> 02:21.770
Whoa!

02:21.770 --> 02:22.320
What is this?

02:26.380 --> 02:28.390
Eureka will catch you cleanly!

02:32.890 --> 02:34.110
Uh... Huh?

02:39.330 --> 02:40.110
Eureka...!

02:41.760 --> 02:42.570
Gotcha!

02:46.380 --> 02:48.590
Who are you? A Pokémon?

02:58.430 --> 02:59.380
So cute!

02:59.680 --> 03:01.630
I have never seen this Pokémon before.

03:01.970 --> 03:03.790
That's right! In times like this...

03:04.110 --> 03:05.120
The newest model!

03:08.110 --> 03:09.180
No data.

03:09.570 --> 03:10.120
Huh?

03:11.200 --> 03:12.270
I'll try too.

03:13.790 --> 03:14.810
No data.

03:15.090 --> 03:16.900
Huh? It really doesn't work...

03:17.250 --> 03:19.860
Does that mean it is a new Pokémon species?!

03:20.190 --> 03:22.110
Awesome! What a huge discovery!

03:22.460 --> 03:23.210
I've decided!

03:25.290 --> 03:26.700
I'll take care of this little one!

03:27.180 --> 03:28.090
What?!

03:28.250 --> 03:31.200
Will you be all right? There are so many things we do not know about it yet!

03:31.840 --> 03:33.580
We will if we take care of it.

03:34.290 --> 03:36.570
If you don't have a name, I'll give you one!

03:37.550 --> 03:39.630
Uhm...

03:39.890 --> 03:40.500
In that case...

03:41.980 --> 03:43.590
It's squishy, so Squishy it is!

03:45.840 --> 03:47.650
"Squishy", huh? That's a nice one!

03:47.650 --> 03:49.020
Nice to meet you, Squishy!

03:49.870 --> 03:53.010
Eureka, <i>your</i> names are nothing but descriptions too...

03:56.850 --> 03:58.450
You're its senior, Dedenne, so I'll count on you!

04:08.860 --> 04:09.680
Dodrio!

04:14.610 --> 04:15.370
And a Juptile!

04:20.300 --> 04:20.960
You are...!

04:21.100 --> 04:23.360
Juptile!

04:24.910 --> 04:26.200
Please wait!

04:26.910 --> 04:27.720
Uh, huh?

04:28.650 --> 04:29.450
Shota!

04:32.300 --> 04:33.690
It has been a while!

04:34.270 --> 04:35.790
What was that just now?

04:36.290 --> 04:37.920
I was trying to get one of them.

04:37.920 --> 04:39.450
So that's why you were running after them.

04:41.020 --> 04:43.040
Hey, Squishy is gone!

04:43.040 --> 04:43.630
What?!

04:44.080 --> 04:45.320
"Squishy"?

05:06.510 --> 05:07.440
Oh my!

05:07.980 --> 05:09.790
Gotcha, Z-chan!

05:10.670 --> 05:12.210
Disperse! Surround it!

05:12.430 --> 05:12.930
Understood!

05:14.140 --> 05:16.310
This is Correa. Momiji, go ahead.

05:17.420 --> 05:19.290
This is Momiji. What do you want?

05:20.170 --> 05:22.300
How did the capture of Z-2 go?

05:22.800 --> 05:24.010
It got away.

05:24.010 --> 05:25.820
Oh my, too bad for you!

05:26.590 --> 05:29.740
Then I'll get Z-1 first!

05:31.970 --> 05:33.260
Squishy!

05:33.770 --> 05:34.910
Squishy!

05:35.250 --> 05:36.640
Squishy!

05:36.640 --> 05:37.850
Hey!

05:38.510 --> 05:39.910
Come back!

05:40.770 --> 05:43.090
Shota, thank you for helping.

05:43.420 --> 05:46.450
It is nothing. I want to meet Squishy, too.

05:46.780 --> 05:48.170
Pikachu, how are things looking up there?

05:58.060 --> 05:59.090
My, my.

06:00.620 --> 06:03.450
You're such a bad child, running away like that, Z-chan.

06:05.090 --> 06:06.720
Dorapion, Pin Missile!

06:12.480 --> 06:13.150
Don't tell me that's...

06:17.520 --> 06:19.520
Come on, let's return to the laboratory.

06:21.760 --> 06:22.590
Squishy!

06:22.590 --> 06:23.830
What are you guys doing?

06:24.080 --> 06:25.710
What do you want, boys and girls?

06:25.710 --> 06:27.170
Let that Pokémon go!

06:27.520 --> 06:28.720
"Pokémon"...?

06:29.650 --> 06:30.720
Well, I guess you could call it that.

06:30.970 --> 06:32.300
It doesn't like what you're doing to it!

06:32.850 --> 06:36.860
Oh my! What we do with our little one is our choice, right?!

06:39.790 --> 06:40.810
"Our little one"...?

06:43.470 --> 06:46.130
You're wrong! Squishy is crying for help!

06:46.410 --> 06:47.560
I can tell!

06:48.210 --> 06:50.160
Who on earth are you guys?!

06:50.750 --> 06:52.690
Argh! This is getting bothersome.

06:53.070 --> 06:54.250
Dorapion, Toxic!

06:56.540 --> 06:58.190
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

07:05.010 --> 07:05.630
Juptile,

07:06.060 --> 07:07.410
Leaf Storm!

07:15.530 --> 07:16.800
I'll catch you, Squishy!

07:18.240 --> 07:19.580
Go get 'em, you guys!

07:20.330 --> 07:21.420
Onbat, please!

07:24.670 --> 07:25.420
Supersonic!

07:29.740 --> 07:30.460
Now you've done it...!

07:30.810 --> 07:31.790
Sludge Bomb!

07:32.720 --> 07:33.760
Thunderbolt!

07:46.960 --> 07:49.120
Hm, not bad.

07:51.360 --> 07:52.530
Pokémon Quiz!

07:52.930 --> 07:53.770
The answer is...?

08:05.050 --> 08:10.560
I can't believe you both let Z get away. There's a limit to how stupid it's possible to be.

08:11.050 --> 08:12.170
I'm so sorry.

08:12.590 --> 08:14.060
I'll continue searching.

08:14.060 --> 08:17.980
Wait. Akebi and Bara have received marching orders too.

08:18.960 --> 08:20.960
We were pretty busy too, you know.

08:21.210 --> 08:24.040
It sucks that we have to clean up after you.

08:24.560 --> 08:25.690
Play nice.

08:27.100 --> 08:28.540
This is Z.

08:28.540 --> 08:30.490
This is its centrosome, Core,

08:30.490 --> 08:31.870
and these are its somata, Cell.

08:32.410 --> 08:35.410
This Core is what you will search for and secure.

08:36.380 --> 08:37.690
At present, there are two Cores.

08:38.330 --> 08:41.180
The first to be discovered was the one codenamed Z-1.

08:41.730 --> 08:44.480
It's the one that escaped from this laboratory earlier.

08:45.890 --> 08:50.210
The one that was confirmed next is codenamed Z-2.

08:55.560 --> 08:57.660
Then I'll take Z-1.

08:57.980 --> 09:00.700
Fine with me. I'll take Z-2.

09:01.200 --> 09:04.480
They should've left it to us from the start.

09:04.830 --> 09:06.530
It's too much for Momiji and Correa...

09:06.860 --> 09:07.700
Right?

09:07.950 --> 09:08.970
Shut up!

09:09.370 --> 09:11.210
I'll be sure to catch Z-1...

09:15.870 --> 09:17.210
What on earth was that?

09:17.500 --> 09:20.090
Hey, I think Squishy is unharmed.

09:20.620 --> 09:21.760
Thank goodness.

09:22.300 --> 09:25.610
Squishy, you were telling me to help you, right?

09:29.820 --> 09:31.690
Let us camp here tonight.

09:32.060 --> 09:33.860
All right, everyone! Come out!

09:34.210 --> 09:34.610
Here goes!

09:40.530 --> 09:43.150
Whoa! An Eievui and an Onbat!

09:43.410 --> 09:44.960
So you have got more partners now!

09:44.960 --> 09:45.450
Yeah.

09:45.860 --> 09:47.950
Squishy, these are all our friends.

09:48.450 --> 09:49.470
Make sure to get along.

10:04.350 --> 10:04.830
What do you think?

10:06.640 --> 10:08.210
Do you not want to eat that, Squishy?

10:12.240 --> 10:13.730
Thanks, you two.

10:15.930 --> 10:17.530
Huh? Berries are no good either?

10:18.000 --> 10:19.200
How mysterious.

10:19.840 --> 10:21.630
Squishy, don't you get hungry?

10:29.900 --> 10:31.170
I wonder what it's doing.

10:51.230 --> 10:52.940
Maybe the sun is its food?

10:53.340 --> 10:54.610
That's so convenient!

10:55.130 --> 10:57.710
I wonder what those guys in the red suits were about.

10:58.210 --> 11:02.440
They said it was "their little one", but it sure did not look that way.

11:09.130 --> 11:10.480
Shota, you're good!

11:10.940 --> 11:13.290
I will go do some research about Squishy as well.

11:13.970 --> 11:17.180
I was thinking about asking the Leaders of the Gyms I end up visiting, too.

11:17.180 --> 11:18.510
That's a nice idea!

11:18.810 --> 11:21.370
Oh, Shota, how many Gyms have you been to?

11:21.900 --> 11:23.470
I have been to many.

11:24.080 --> 11:25.200
I have five badges right now.

11:25.870 --> 11:26.540
You, Satoshi?

11:27.870 --> 11:28.970
I have seven.

11:29.280 --> 11:32.190
Ah, I have got to hand it to you. You only have one left to go, huh?

11:32.190 --> 11:32.430
Yeah!

11:36.530 --> 11:39.440
This is the Psychic Badge, right? The one from the Hyakkoku Gym?

11:39.680 --> 11:41.780
Yeah. Gojika-san was strong!

11:43.730 --> 11:45.580
Pikachu deserves a lot of credit for that victory.

11:46.350 --> 11:48.650
That is the one I intend to challenge next.

11:49.180 --> 11:50.030
What is your next, Satoshi?

11:50.690 --> 11:51.540
The Eisetsu Gym.

11:52.030 --> 11:53.520
Eisetsu...

11:57.120 --> 11:58.140
That is this place, huh?

11:58.140 --> 11:59.010
Shota, have you been there?

11:59.410 --> 11:59.760
No.

12:00.090 --> 12:02.810
It seems like a really strong Gym, so I am not ready for that yet.

12:03.520 --> 12:04.290
Oh, but...

12:04.880 --> 12:09.430
...I do recommend the Terminus Cave that is located on the way to Eisetsu.

12:10.270 --> 12:11.840
By Terminus Cave,

12:12.220 --> 12:12.890
you mean this, right?

12:14.880 --> 12:16.240
That's right! It's this one.

12:16.730 --> 12:19.150
There are many Pokémon that you cannot find anywhere else.

12:19.660 --> 12:21.900
Satoshi, this is your chance to get them.

12:22.170 --> 12:23.980
Wow, sounds fun!

12:23.980 --> 12:26.030
Eureka, it's a cave!

12:27.470 --> 12:28.290
A cave?

12:33.150 --> 12:34.830
Hey, hey! Don't jump on that!

12:36.250 --> 12:37.630
Could it be angry?

12:37.630 --> 12:39.790
Is it trying to tell us something, maybe?

12:42.450 --> 12:44.350
Squishy, you want to go there, right?

12:45.170 --> 12:45.840
I knew it!

12:46.290 --> 12:47.310
Right, Squishy?

12:49.580 --> 12:51.690
Shall we go to this Terminus Cave, then?

12:51.920 --> 12:52.290
Yeah!

12:52.970 --> 12:55.850
We might get to learn a little bit about Squishy, after all!

12:56.060 --> 12:56.540
Yeah.

13:26.270 --> 13:27.050
Squishy?

13:27.050 --> 13:28.340
What? What's wrong?

13:30.970 --> 13:32.300
Wait, Squishy!

13:33.050 --> 13:34.480
Hey, what's the matter?

13:37.370 --> 13:38.650
Squishy!

13:42.830 --> 13:43.270
Watch out!

13:43.770 --> 13:45.200
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

13:46.130 --> 13:47.760
Juptile, Leaf Blade!

13:59.280 --> 14:00.300
It's those guys from earlier...

14:00.830 --> 14:02.270
Gekogashira, help us out!

14:05.230 --> 14:06.170
Tairenar, please!

14:06.170 --> 14:07.680
Rentorar, please come out!

14:10.830 --> 14:12.610
Are you all right? You're not injured, are you?

14:13.980 --> 14:16.330
Oh my... Leave us be, will you?!

14:16.640 --> 14:18.100
I told you this was <i>our</i> little one!

14:18.410 --> 14:19.360
We won't leave you be!

14:19.740 --> 14:22.890
"Our little one, our little one", yeah right! It doesn't look like you're treating it kindly!

14:23.170 --> 14:24.310
I do not think so either!

14:24.790 --> 14:27.200
Oh my, you kids really are bothersome!

14:27.660 --> 14:28.670
Cross Poison!

14:30.720 --> 14:31.490
Dark Pulse!

14:32.700 --> 14:34.590
Gekogashira, Water Pulse!

14:34.810 --> 14:36.530
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

14:39.340 --> 14:40.350
Flamethrower!

14:42.090 --> 14:43.900
Rentorar, Swift!

14:49.840 --> 14:52.560
Serena, Citron, take Eureka and Squishy and run!

14:53.230 --> 14:55.050
Please leave this to us!

14:55.440 --> 14:57.790
Satoshi, Shota, take it easy.

14:57.790 --> 14:58.560
Got it.

14:59.970 --> 15:01.420
Please return, Rentorar!

15:01.610 --> 15:02.750
Tairenar, return!

15:04.140 --> 15:05.310
What? What?

15:05.570 --> 15:07.050
There was a flicker of electricity.

15:07.410 --> 15:08.850
Then it might be Pikachu!

15:09.120 --> 15:10.530
Let's rush there right away!

15:12.640 --> 15:13.550
Yay!

15:27.100 --> 15:28.000
Oh no!

15:28.590 --> 15:30.010
We need to run after Eureka and the others!

15:32.530 --> 15:34.170
Are you two all right?

15:34.510 --> 15:35.210
Yeah.

15:35.420 --> 15:36.530
Come on, Eureka.

15:37.840 --> 15:39.070
Squishy is gone!

15:58.860 --> 15:59.710
We won't let you get away.

16:00.400 --> 16:02.910
We still have some experiments for you to go through!

17:03.130 --> 17:04.090
What's this?!

17:04.330 --> 17:05.810
No one told me about this!

17:12.800 --> 17:13.390
Fall back!

17:16.780 --> 17:17.400
Squishy?!

17:18.000 --> 17:19.180
It must be Squishy!

17:19.570 --> 17:20.560
Wait, Eureka!

17:23.250 --> 17:23.840
What is that?

17:24.220 --> 17:24.800
Let's go!

17:44.490 --> 17:45.340
Squishy!

17:46.480 --> 17:48.290
What is this? What is going on?

17:48.530 --> 17:49.650
Serena! Citron!

17:49.900 --> 17:50.880
Is everyone all right?

17:51.210 --> 17:51.900
Where are those guys?

17:52.320 --> 17:53.270
They seem to be gone.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.860
Are you all right, Squishy?

18:07.990 --> 18:08.750
Squishy...

18:11.370 --> 18:12.060
I'm sorry.

18:12.850 --> 18:14.250
I won't let you go any more.

18:15.470 --> 18:16.960
Thank goodness everyone's all right.

18:17.330 --> 18:19.920
Shota, you fighting alongside us was of great help.

18:20.210 --> 18:22.730
Do you think Juptile and I made a difference?

18:25.120 --> 18:26.140
Of course!

18:27.340 --> 18:28.540
Thank you very much!

18:28.910 --> 18:30.560
Thank you for the EXP!

18:41.250 --> 18:43.530
Z has another form.

18:45.170 --> 18:48.000
This is critical information to Operation Z.

18:48.780 --> 18:50.210
We need to report this to headquarters...

18:59.020 --> 19:00.170
That was close.

19:00.170 --> 19:01.790
They're pretty perceptive.

19:01.790 --> 19:03.260
They mentioned a "Z".

19:06.430 --> 19:08.480
Don't yell! Don't talk! Don't jump out!

19:09.280 --> 19:11.840
I have a feeling trouble's brewing... It's a good feeling.

19:20.210 --> 19:23.370
Gojika, the Gym Leader of the Hyakkoku Gym, said:

19:24.810 --> 19:28.670
"In the near future, I see Kalos in an unprecedented crisis."

19:29.820 --> 19:31.470
"Green flames will waver..."

19:32.110 --> 19:35.710
"...and wrap itself around humans and Pokémon."

19:37.360 --> 19:39.650
But Satoshi and his friends don't yet know...

19:40.510 --> 19:43.850
...that they are already caught up in the vortex of this incident.

19:53.010 --> 19:56.090
What is awaiting them down the road?

19:56.970 --> 19:57.930
To be continued...

20:03.970 --> 20:06.530
This is a Z we didn't know about yet!

20:07.710 --> 20:10.730
This means we don't know everything Z is capable of.

20:11.850 --> 20:13.120
Hurry up and recover it.

20:13.360 --> 20:13.680
Sir!

20:16.540 --> 20:19.870
We'll have info on further giveaways shortly after this!

20:20.840 --> 20:25.790
Sunday November 1st at 8am!

20:21.950 --> 20:24.060
Pokénchi airs on Sundays at 8 AM!

20:24.060 --> 20:25.500
Makunoshita!

20:28.570 --> 20:30.170
I love Pikachu!

20:31.270 --> 20:34.630
This is a program about Pikachu lovers for Pikachu lovers brought to you by Pikachu lovers:

20:34.630 --> 20:36.010
"I love Pikachu!"

20:36.200 --> 20:38.230
I've discovered another cute Pikachu!

20:39.480 --> 20:42.030
This Pikachu belongs to a Trainer from Masara Town!

20:42.270 --> 20:45.930
Its cheeks that store electricity and the shape of its tail are the greatest, don't you agree?

20:47.420 --> 20:52.010
Apparently, it doesn't go in its ball but always stays by its Trainer's side and acts in concert with him.

20:52.010 --> 20:53.500
So cute!

20:53.500 --> 20:57.450
This is how it gives electric massages to its Trainer!

20:57.450 --> 20:59.100
That's kinda nice!

20:59.100 --> 21:01.500
We gotta keep watching this Pikachu!

21:02.860 --> 21:04.360
Pikachu's funny faces!

21:10.940 --> 21:12.670
Who is it imitating?

21:12.890 --> 21:13.790
The correct answer is...

21:15.820 --> 21:18.570
Now then, see you next Pikachu!

21:18.570 --> 21:19.480
Bye-bye!

21:23.030 --> 21:24.970
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:25.150 --> 21:26.350
Towards our next adventure!

21:26.910 --> 21:29.310
A wild Hariborg has fallen in love with Eievui at first sight?!

21:29.720 --> 21:34.810
It pursues it relentlessly in all kinds of ways, but that might end up having the opposite effect on the shy Eievui...

21:35.340 --> 21:37.150
What? Now you want a battle?

21:37.480 --> 21:39.180
You want to show how strong you are?

21:39.710 --> 21:41.770
Uhm... I'm not sure about that...

21:41.990 --> 21:44.490
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:44.760 --> 21:47.300
Hot-blooded Hariborg! Squishy is Being Targeted!

21:47.300 --> 21:50.860
Next Time

21:47.300 --> 21:50.860
Hot-blooded Hariborg!
Squishy is Being Targeted!

21:47.900 --> 21:49.610
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:51.930 --> 21:54.590
The data broadcast giveaways are not over yet!

21:55.350 --> 21:57.230
Next week, you can receive an alternate-colored Yveltal...

21:57.870 --> 21:59.510
...and the week after, you can receive Zygarde!

22:00.270 --> 22:03.450
Everyone, get Pokémon with the data broadcast!

22:03.810 --> 22:18.780
Next episode:

22:03.810 --> 22:11.290
A Hariborg appears!

22:04.730 --> 22:08.110
This program was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:11.320 --> 22:18.780
It falls in love with Eievui at first sight!?
